# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Google PageSpeed Insights API key — powers /analyze
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Without a key, requests fall into Google's shared anonymous pool and fail
# with "Quota exceeded ... for consumer project_number:583797351490" at
# unpredictable times. With one you get 25,000 requests/day free, no card.
#
#   1. https://console.cloud.google.com -> create or pick a project
#   2. APIs & Services -> Library -> "PageSpeed Insights API" -> Enable
#   3. APIs & Services -> Credentials -> Create credentials -> API key
#
# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE DEPLOYING
#
# The PUBLIC_ prefix is not decorative. Astro inlines any PUBLIC_* variable
# into the JavaScript bundle the browser downloads, because /analyze calls
# Google directly from the visitor's browser. Keeping this file out of git does
# NOT keep the key secret in production — anyone can open devtools and read it.
#
# That is acceptable ONLY if the key is restricted, which you must do in the
# Google Cloud console on the key itself:
#
#   Application restrictions -> Websites
#       https://websetly.com/*
#       https://*.websetly.com/*
#   API restrictions -> Restrict key -> PageSpeed Insights API
#
# Unrestricted, the key gets scraped out of the bundle and someone else burns
# your daily quota.
#
# Set the same variable in the Cloudflare Pages environment for production.
PSI_API_KEY=
